details:
(a) whether the Archaeological Survey of India (ASI) is drawing on international best practices, expert agencies and partner countries in monument conservation and if so, the details thereof; 
(b) the number of vacancies in the ASI and the adequacy of its human resources; and 
(c) the steps being taken to attract younger generation to archaeology and conservation, as a career?

(a) whether Government has assessed the trend of increasing concentration of rainfall in fewer days, resulting in a decline in the number of wet days and an increase in dry days and the extreme-weather implications thereby; 
(b) the details of frequency of extreme-weather-event days during the last five years; and 
(c) the adaptation measures being planned in response?

(a) the gross revenue and Adjusted Gross Revenue (AGR) of all the telecom service providers during the year ending March, 2026, total and operator-wise; 
(b) the spectrum usage charges levied by Government for the same period; 
(c) the current status of AGR issues and the outstanding AGR dues with telecom and non-telecom service providers, total and operator/provider-wise; and 
(d) the details of relief extended in respect of AGR dues to telecom operators other than Vodafone Idea, and the manner in which Government's investment and equity stake is protected thereby?

(a) the comparative performance of States under Mission Shakti and the parameters used for such comparison;
(b) the performance of Odisha under the Mission during the period 2020 to 2024 and thereafter; and
(c) the outcomes achieved against the expenditure incurred?

(a) whether Government is aware that many eligible beneficiaries in Odisha are yet to receive ration cards under the National Food Security Act (NFSA);
(b) whether any assessment has been made of eligible households awaiting inclusion under the NFSA;
(c) whether Government proposes to enhance State-wise NFSA coverage to include all eligible beneficiaries;
(d) the steps taken to ensure transparent and timely issuance of ration cards; and
(e) the details of beneficiaries covered, pending applications and additional allocations made to Odisha during the last three years?

(a) whether the Central Government has received any proposal for the planned development of Cuttack, including the New Cuttack urban expansion project;
(b) whether financial assistance has been sanctioned for roads, drainage, sanitation and flood management infrastructure;
(c) whether the status of urban infrastructure projects sanctioned during the last three years has been reviewed;
(d) whether any fresh proposal is under consideration for integrated urban development under any Central Scheme; and
(e) the details of projects sanctioned, funds released and works completed during the last three years?

(a) whether Government is aware that the State of Odisha continues to suffer extensive damage to its power transmission and distribution infrastructure during major cyclones;
(b) whether a proposal from Government of Odisha seeking a special power infrastructure package of ?10,000 crore after Cyclone Yaas has been received;
(c) whether the proposal has been examined and the outcome thereof;
(d) the reasons for its non-sanction or delay, if any; and
(e) whether Government proposes to reconsider the proposal or provide alternative financial assistance for resilient power infrastructure?

(a) whether Government is aware that MSMEs in Odisha face delays in obtaining statutory approvals from various departments;
(b) whether the effectiveness of the existing Single Window System has been reviewed for providing time-bound clearances;
(c) whether any proposal is under consideration for a fully integrated digital Single Window platform with prescribed timelines;
(d) whether State Governments, industry bodies and MSME associations have been consulted on simplifying regulatory approvals; and
(e) the measures taken to improve Ease of Doing Business and promote industrial investment in Odisha during the last three years?

(a) whether Government has assessed the availability and requirement of cold storage infrastructure in Odisha, particularly in major agricultural and horticultural districts;
(b) the number and storage capacity of cold storage facilities in the State, district-wise;
(c) whether additional cold storage units are proposed under any Central Sector or Centrally Sponsored Scheme (CSS);
(d) the details of financial assistance provided for development of cold chain infrastructure in Odisha during the last five years; and
(e) the measures taken to strengthen post-harvest management and agricultural marketing infrastructure in the State?

(a) whether Government is aware that migration of workers from Odisha to other States continues despite industrial and mineral development in the State;
(b) whether any assessment has been made of employment generated for local youth by industries in Odisha;
(c) whether any policy requires industries to provide employment opportunities to local residents;
(d) the measures taken to reduce distress migration through skill development, employment generation and livelihood promotion; and
(e) the details of migrant workers from Odisha registered under Central welfare schemes during the last three years?
SR

(a) whether Government has taken note of increasing traffic congestion, road accidents and urban mobility challenges in Bhubaneswar and Cuttack due to rapid urbanisation and inadequate road infrastructure;
(b) whether any proposal has been received from Government of Odisha for construction of elevated corridors, flyovers or other traffic decongestion projects in these cities;
(c) whether any feasibility study has been conducted for such projects;
(d) the details of Central assistance sanctioned or proposed for improving urban road infrastructure in Odisha under various schemes; and
(e) the details of measures taken to improve traffic management and road safety in Bhubaneswar and Cuttack?
GK

(a) whether Government has considered a graded or targeted fertilizer subsidy calibrated to farmers' land-holding, so that support is better directed towards small and marginal farmers;
(b) the details or present status of any such proposal; and
(c) whether the imbalance in nutrient use arising from the disproportionately low price of urea under the Nutrient Based Subsidy regime is being addressed and the manner thereof?

(a) whether an independent evaluation has been carried out for measurable outcomes delivered by the Smart Cities Mission (SCM) against the expenditure incurred;
(b) the most significant and replicable benefits that have actually accrued to citizens;
(c) whether any independent studies have been conducted to find out if smart cities that have reported flooding during rainfall incidents; and
(d) whether a roadmap exists for sustaining and scaling these interventions following the conclusion of the mission, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of Global Capability Centres (GCCs) operating in the country and the workforce they have hired;
(b) the incentives offered to them and the measures taken to promote the hiring of entry-level talent with the requisite upskilling; and
(c) the Government's vision for the expansion of GCC hubs, including to States beyond the established metros?

(a) the targets set for enhancing the share of nuclear energy in the country's energy mix during the next two decades;
(b) the details of vision regarding Small Modular Reactors, including any international partnerships for technology transfer; and
(c) the timeframe and estimated cost for deploying the first indigenous Small Modular Reactors?

(a) how teachers are being prepared to train students in artificial intelligence and emerging technologies and the state of the requisite school infrastructure;
(b) whether the curriculum framework is agile enough to update rapidly, rather than straitjacketing learning to fixed syllabi;
(c) whether a protocol, in line with international standards, governs the responsible use and self-declaration of artificial intelligence in research theses and dissertations; and
(d) the details thereof?

(a) the present number of hospital beds and doctors per thousand population, separately for urban and rural areas, and how these compare with World Health Organization norms and comparable economies;
(b) whether Government has assessed the urban-rural imbalance in access to healthcare;
(c) whether a white paper or long-term roadmap on the future of healthcare in the country, addressing populations with poor access, has been prepared or is proposed; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of cases of diversion, black-marketing or leakage of subsidised fertilizers detected in the country, including in Odisha, over the last three years;
(b) the quantum of subsidy estimated to have been lost due to black-marketing and diversion;
(c) whether the sale of fertilizers through PoS devices under Direct Benefit Transfer has demonstrably curbed such diversion; and
(d) the grievance-redressal avenue available to a farmer denied fertilizer at the notified price?
SR

(a) the projected year-on-year growth in peak power demand, including the additional load anticipated from artificial-intelligence data centres, and whether captive or renewable capacity serving such centres will be connected to the grid;
(b) whether investment in grid modernisation and transmission is keeping pace with investment in generation capacity, the details thereof;
(c) whether investment in coal- and gas-based capacity is presently growing faster than renewable capacity; and
(d) the steps being taken to ensure inter-ministerial coherence in the country's power strategy?

(a) the number of startups and incubators supported in Odisha under the Startup India initiative;
(b) the schemes through which startups are funded, whether by way of equity, grant or debt; and
(c) the specific support extended to deep-technology and research-and-development-driven startups?

(a) the overall trend in the country's exports over the last three years;
(b) the major sectors that have suffered an export decline owing to the prevailing geopolitical situation and tariff changes; 
(c) the countries and products in respect of which exports have become easier or more difficult on account of recent tariff and trade-policy shifts; and
(d) the share of manufacturing, services and agriculture respectively in the country’s export and the trend in the last three years in dollar value, till March 2026?

(a) the steps taken to preserve and promote the classical and folk dance and art forms of Odisha, such as Odissi, Gotipua and Chhau;
(b) the mechanism for recognising and supporting artists in both the performing and non-performing arts, including emerging artists; and
(c) the schemes available to curate, train and provide livelihood security to such artists?

(a) the current status of broadband connectivity to all Gram Panchayats (GPs) in Odisha and whether there is 100% coverage for all blocks and GPs and if not, the timeline for completion;
(b) whether the village Padmanabhpur under the Gram Panchayat Machhakote, Ganjam has broadband connectivity; and
(c) whether there have been complaints or representations received by BSNL General Manager Behrampur regarding non availability of broadband due to non availability of OFC route in the region?

(a) whether a maker-checker or independent review system exists to prevent erroneous, outdated or inappropriate content from entering curricula and textbooks;
(b) if so, the details thereof and the number of cases detected in the last three years; and
(c) the steps taken by Government to ensure that the curriculum stays relevant to the future demands of the economy and the global outlook, details of specific steps taken towards ensuring this?

(a) whether any controlled study, using comparable student cohorts, has been undertaken to establish whether performance in competitive examinations differs by the mode of examination, that is, online versus pen-and-paper;
(b) the details thereof, if any;
(c) whether structured counselling and guidance are available in schools to help students cope with the pressure caused by competitive examinations; and
(d) the coverage of such support across Government schools?

(a) whether complaints regarding financial misappropriation or irregularities in the procurement or empanelment processes under the CGHS have been received, if so, the action taken thereon and the number of convictions secured;
(b) whether a mechanism exists for CGHS beneficiaries to lodge complaints regarding denial of admission or delay or dilution of services by empanelled hospitals, delayed reimbursement, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the number of such complaints received during the last three years and the action taken thereon; and
(d) whether any helpline or grievance redressal facility exists for beneficiaries/pensioners facing denial of services at the time of admission, and if so, the details thereof

(a) the net Foreign Portfolio Investment inflows into Indian equity and debt markets, separately, for the last three financial years and for the current financial year up to date;
(b) the cumulative net outflow of Foreign Portfolio Investment during October 2024 to April 2026, in equity and debt markets separately, along with principal triggers identified for such outflows; and
(c) whether Government considers India's substantial reliance on Foreign Portfolio Investment as a financing source for Capital Account, in the context of declining net Foreign Direct Investment, to be sustainable and the structural reforms proposed to deepen the domestic institutional investor base?

(a) the fertilizer subsidy outgo and the share of domestic demand met through imports over the last three years, product-wise (urea, DAP and complex fertilizers);
(b) whether domestic production is keeping pace with the growth in consumption and the projected gap;
(c) the supply-chain risks identified in respect of imported feedstock and finished fertilizers, particularly from a small number of source countries; and
(d) the steps being taken to achieve self-reliance and mitigate such risks?

(a) the present refining capacity of the country in relation to domestic consumption and the extent of refined-product exports;
(b) by when domestic consumption is projected to absorb the present surplus refining capacity;
(c) the achievement under the E20 ethanol-blending target and the roadmap, if any, towards higher ethanol blending; and
(d) whether the land water and food-security implications of higher blending targets have been assessed?

(a) whether the body responsible for investigating aircraft accidents and serious incidents is structurally, financially and operationally independent of the regulator and of the operators it investigates, in keeping with ICAO Annex 13 and international best practice;
(b) the details of its present composition, funding and reporting line; and
(c) if such independence is not fully assured, the reasons therefor and the steps proposed to secure it?
